       "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "What is chronic kidney disease (CKD)? Chronic kidney disease is described as any loss of kidney functioning that develops beyond a 3 month period.\n<p>Sources:\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.kidney.org/atoz/content/about-chronic-kidney-disease\">https://www.kidney.org/atoz/content/about-chronic-kidney-disease</a>\nPathoma by Dr. Sattar (Pg 132-133)\nHarrison’s Principles of Internal Medicine 18th Ed.\nUpToDate\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://emedicine.medscape.com/article/238798-overview#a4\">http://emedicine.medscape.com/article/238798-overview#a4</a>\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(16)32064-5/fulltext\">http://thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(16)32064-5/fulltext</a>\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.kidney.org/sites/default/files/02-10-6785_HBE_Hyperkalemia_Bulletin.pdf\">https://www.kidney.org/sites/default/files/02-10-6785_HBE_Hyperkalemia_Bulletin.pdf</a>\n</p>\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.kidney.org/sites/default/files/01-10-7278_HBG_CKD_Stages_Flyer3.pdf\">https://www.kidney.org/sites/default/files/01-10-7278_HBG_CKD_Stages_Flyer3.pdf</a>",
